{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774056049,"nonce":"Cmci8s69Ou1tjDVvkn4zxhwNDY8=","title":"fix: preset feature integration bugs — startup import, API mismatch, library button styling","message":"Three bugs in the presets feature (Bug: 61bee4e):\n\n1. **importClaudeMd never called on startup**: The function existed in src/presets.ts but was never invoked from src/index.ts during daemon startup. CLAUDE.md files were never auto-imported as presets.\n\n2. **addSessionPreset API mismatch**: Server POST /api/console/sessions/:id/presets expects { presetIds: string[] } but the client sent { preset_id, position }. This caused silent 400 errors, so presets were never added to sessions. Additionally, getSessionPresets expected a bare array but server returns { presets: [...] }, so it always returned []. Also, getPresetUnion returned { text, tokenEstimate } but was cast to { systemPrompt, settingSources, totalTokens } — fields never matched.\n\n3. **Library button invisible text**: The Convention Library button in the Presets sidebar is a \u003cbutton\u003e element whose user-agent styles override inherited color/font properties, making text invisible or wrong color in dark themes.","files":null}]}